{"shortDescription":"The Japanese yen weakened past 154 per dollar on Friday, retreating from near seven-month highs as the dollar recovered after data showed US producer inflation accelerated in August, bolstering bets for a Federal Reserve rate hike next week.The yen also faced pressure from surging oil prices that k…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The Japanese yen weakened past 154 per dollar on Friday, retreating from near seven-month highs as the dollar recovered after data showed US producer inflation accelerated in August, bolstering bets for a Federal Reserve rate hike next week."]},{"type":"p","children":["The yen also faced pressure from surging oil prices that kept inflation risks elevated, with the US and Iran showing no signs of backing down from the war."]},{"type":"p","children":["Meanwhile, data showed Japanese producer inflation climbed 7.6% in August, reinforcing expectations for a Bank of Japan rate increase this month."]},{"type":"p","children":["Sentiment among large manufacturers also improved sharply in Q3, reaching its strongest level since Q4 2021 amid robust government support measures."]},{"type":"p","children":["Still, the yen remained up more than 3% so far this month, supported by expectations for more aggressive BOJ policy tightening, the unwinding of carry trades and increased capital repatriation."]}]},"language":"en","tags":[{"title":"Forex","args":[{"id":"category","value":"forex"}]},{"title":"Trading Economics","args":[{"id":"provider","value":"trading-economics"}]}],"id":"te_news:582961:0","title":"Yen Weakens as Dollar Rebounds","published":1789091448,"urgency":2,"link":"https://tradingeconomics.com/japan/currency","permission":"preview","relatedSymbols":[{"symbol":"FX:USDJPY","currency-logoid":"country/JP","base-currency-logoid":"country/US","logo":{"style":"pair","logoid":"country/US","logoid2":"country/JP"}},{"symbol":"FTMO_OANDA:USDJPY.SIM","currency-logoid":"country/JP","base-currency-